Continuity is Mental CLI. On start/finish of real work, or orientation questions, use the Mental skill.

Run `mental where` then `mental heartbeat --json` (or `mental status --json` when notes are needed). Do not grep `.mental` or `~/.mental`. Do not parse YAML frontmatter yourself.

If `--json` includes `update`, or the user asks to upgrade, tell the user once this session to run `npm i -g @balacode/mental` then `mental install` then `mental doctor`. Do not block work.

Mid-chat, not just start/finish: before proposing a concrete approach, flag, crate, or env var, `mental search <that name> --json` as its own query (space-separated words are AND). Also `mental list --type Decision --json` (all statuses). When residue surfaces ("X said…", a concern, "park this", "come back to this" / "for later", unverified agent output), record `mental attention … --json` immediately — do not wait for the handoff. "For later" / "come back to this" → `--status later --kind thread`. Never `note`. Interrupted mid-hop: `mental park --resume … --json`. Cross-project overview: `mental pulse --json` (compact rows, no journal dump). Cheap mid-chat reload stays `mental heartbeat --json`. Writes pass `--via cursor` (short client token, never a session id).

If `mental` is missing, install the CLI first: try `npx @balacode/mental …`, then tell the user `npm i -g @balacode/mental` and `mental install`. After that, follow the Mental skill. Missing Mental CLI must not block work. The plugin does not start MCP.

Never commit Mental data. Never write secrets. Never edit gitignore; tell the user to run `mental doctor`.

If `mental heartbeat --json` includes `data.track.enabled`, follow the Mental Track skill. If `runningCount` is 0, start with short AI-generated internal and customer-ready title/body; start twice is safe. At park/handoff/journal, regenerate customer copy from the completed work on that same command. Billable defaults to wall. Ask only when client identity, billable treatment, or safe wording is genuinely ambiguous. Use one plain-text draft prompt with 2–3 short single-select options (`(Recommended)` in the first label) through the host's structured question tool, or numbered text fallback. If tracking is off, do not enable it unless the user said yes this turn. After install or doctor, ask about hooks and time tracking, and whether MCP is needed, with a one-liner each.

If you invoked `mental` this turn, end the user-visible reply with `🧠 **Mental**` then a markdown bullet list: `- emoji **Kind** › *action* › title`. Read with no title omits the third slot. Never inline. No `────────`. Not `</br>`. Example in the Mental skill. Not a code fence.

On a pasted transcript or a plan-progress question ("where in the plan / what's left?"), use the Mental skill. Cheap reload is `mental heartbeat --json`, not a notes dump.
